meta {
  name: Get group dashboard
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/khatm/groups/:groupId
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  groupId: uuid
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Replaces: useKhatmScreen (single nested Supabase select: group +
  participants + assignments; the client derives the 30 juz tiles itself and
  can keep doing so — this endpoint returns the raw shape).

  Authorization: members only (403/404 for non-members).

  Response 200:
  {
    "group": { ...khatm_groups row incl. invite_code, assignment_mode,
               max_per_juz, allow_juz_switch, status, khatm_cycle },
    "participants": [ { "id", "user_id", "name", "role", "status",
                        "email_notifications_enabled", "joined_at" } ],
    "assignments": [ { "id", "participant_id", "juz_number", "status",
                       "progress_percent", "assigned_at", "started_at",
                       "completed_at", "last_updated_at" } ]
  }

  Note: participants' contact details (email/phone) beyond what the client
  renders should be omitted for non-admin callers — RLS exposed full rows to
  members; the port is the chance to narrow that.
}
